{"operations":[{"content":"def chunk(data, size):\n    \"\"\"Yield successive chunks from data of given size.\n\n    If size is larger than the length of data, yield one chunk containing all data.\n    The final chunk may be smaller than size if data length is not a multiple of size.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"chunk size must be positive\")\n    length = len(data)\n    if length == 0:\n        return []\n    if size >= length:\n        yield data\n        return\n    for i in range(0, length, size):\n        yield data[i:i + size]\n","expected_sha256":"eed9426a1a922d15bf28fddd756f2a2b2feb15688c0414a9aa0e740c3bcf997d","kind":"modify","path":"src/chunking.py"}],"rationale":"Changed the empty data case to return an empty list instead of returning None to satisfy tests expecting a list. Kept the rest of the logic as is, which already yields the final partial chunk and yields one chunk if size is larger than input length. Added raising ValueError for non-positive size as required."}